  "summary": {
    "tldr": "Adds a usage-based pricing tier with metered execution and monthly invoicing. Two new tables, a nightly rollup cron, and Stripe invoice writes; the new tier is opt-in only so no production backfill is required.",
    "ships": [
      "Usage-based pricing tier (opt-in) selectable from the Admin Billing UI.",
      "`usage_meter_events` + `usage_invoices` tables in Postgres.",
      "Nightly cron rolls meter events into invoice line items.",
      "`/billing/usage` REST endpoints + tier-switch logic in the Billing API."
    ],
    "why": "Existing tier is flat-rate only; no path to bill heavy users proportionally.",
    "changes": [
      "Two new tables; existing `tenants.tier` widens to include the new value.",
      "Stripe invoice writes are not yet idempotent in v1 \u2014 dedupe by `(tenant, period_start)`.",
      "Cron must deploy AFTER the migration \u2014 references new tables."
    ]
  },
